within Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.C_CardiovascularSystem.C08C_SelectiveCalciumChannelBlockersWithMainlyVascula.C08CA05_Nifedipine;
model Nifedipine "Nifedipine — default model: Nifedipine_Fu2022_reference"
  extends Nifedipine_Fu2022_reference;
  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>The default model of nifedipine: <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.C_CardiovascularSystem.C08C_SelectiveCalciumChannelBlockersWithMainlyVascula.C08CA05_Nifedipine.Nifedipine_Fu2022_reference\">Nifedipine_Fu2022_reference</a>, chosen among the models extracted from papers (reviewer verdict, ground-truth agreement, completeness). All models of nifedipine in this package:</p><ul><li><code>Nifedipine_Fu2022_reference</code></li><li><code>Nifedipine_Kiriyama2024_PD_bp</code></li><li><code>Nifedipine_Kiriyama2024_PD_hr</code></li><li><code>Nifedipine_Kiriyama2024_PD_qt</code></li></ul><h4>About nifedipine</h4><p>Nifedipine is a calcium channel blocker used to treat high blood pressure and angina. It is widely used and appears on the WHO list of essential medicines, and is also being investigated for other uses.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q39111\">Wikidata Q39111</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><p>Identity, molar mass and metabolites: <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.Substances.Nifedipine\">Nifedipine</a>.</p></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from default: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: default</li></ul></body></html>"), experiment(StartTime = 0, StopTime = 604800, Tolerance = 1e-9, Interval = 1));
end Nifedipine;
